  "description": "An application for a non-material amendment under Section 96A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 in connection with the planning permission DC/19/113542 dated 29 April 2021 for the construction of a two storey school building and single storey ancillary buildings to provide a satellite site for the expansion of Greenvale Special Educational Needs Secondary School, being D1 (educational) floorspace including a staff terrace with roof level plant and photo-voltaic panels, together with associated provision of sub-station, sprinkler plant enclosure, pedestrian and vehicle accesss arrangements with canopy cover, vehicle parking, cycle parking, external play space, hard and soft landscaping, and associated ancillary works at the former Brent Knoll School, Mayow Road, SE23 in order to: amend the layout of the external plant enclosurerelocate pump housing to western end of enclosure and add double accesss doorsrelocate sprinker tank to eastern end of enclosure and relocate access doorschange design and materials of vehicle access gates and associated entrance screen to pupil drop off area.",
